  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown below, the switch $\\mathrm{S}$ is connected to position $\\mathrm{P}$ for a long time so that the charge on the capacitor becomes $q_{1} \\mu \\mathrm{C}$. Then $\\mathrm{S}$ is switched to position $\\mathrm{Q}$. After a long time, the charge on the capacitor is $q_{2} \\mu \\mathrm{C}$.<br><img src=\"assets\\qt0004_6114cb1822a0.png\"><br>The magnitude of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.67",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;is connected to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0004_12ce070f4421.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Now, after distribution of potential,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>&#956;F</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.67</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p>"
